==Trivia==
* This card's effect is similar to that of the {{TCG|Unidentified Fossil}} card in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]], but has 40 HP instead of 60 HP and only {{TCGP|Aerodactyl}} can evolve from.
** {{TCG|Old Amber}} also exists in the Pokémon Trading Card Game, but has 50 HP and also has a {{TCG|Poké-Body}}.
{{outdated|section|needs=Info of what happens after Deluxe Pack: ex}}
*The {{TCGP|Mythical Island}} print of this card is exactly the same as the {{TCGP|Genetic Apex}} print, and thus, unlike other cards, an Old Amber card from any booster packs would be considered for both, including for {{TCGP|Mission}}s. This was identified as a bug in an in-game notice published on December 17, 2024.<ref name="MythicalIslandNotices" />

===Origin===
*This card's illustration was first featured on {{TCG ID|Fates Collide|Old Amber Aerodactyl|106}} from the {{TCG|Fates Collide}} expansion.
*An [[Old Amber]] is a [[fossil]] in the [[Pokémon games]] which can be revived into {{p|Aerodactyl}}.

